powerpc64le: a native VSX backend for Embree's 4-wide SIMD layer.

Applies on top of embree-ppc64le.patch (the port itself: CMake detection,
the __SSE*__ ISA switch, the compat-header shim).  This patch is kept
separate because the base port is a self-contained upstreamable change and
stays the fallback: the CMake option added here, EMBREE_PPC64LE_NATIVE_VSX
(default ON on ppc64le), selects between the two; OFF rebuilds 4.4.1-1
exactly.  The PKGBUILD exposes it as _embree_vsx=native|sse.

What it replaces.  With the base patch, Embree's SSE4.2 kernels compile
through GCC's <xmmintrin.h>..<nmmintrin.h> for powerpc64le: every
_mm_shuffle_ps becomes a control-vector load plus xxperm/vperm, every
_mm_blendv_ps an xxsel, every lane extraction a round trip, and nothing in
the SIMD abstraction is written for the machine.  With this patch the four
4-wide types (vfloat4, vint4, vuint4, vboolf4 -- common/simd/*_vsx.h), the
SSE-backed math types (Vec3fa/Vec3fx, Vec3ia, Vec3ba, Vec2fa, Color/Color4
-- common/math/*_vsx.h) and the scalar helpers in emath.h are written on
__vector float/int storage, GCC vector extensions and the altivec builtins.
No x86 SIMD intrinsic exists in the build: <immintrin.h> is never included,
so any surviving _mm_* is a compile error.  The only x86 spellings kept are
the non-SIMD platform hints Embree's system layer calls by name (_mm_pause,
_mm_mfence, _mm_prefetch, _mm_malloc/_mm_free, the MXCSR accessors), defined
in common/simd/vsx/vsx.h.

Design (common/simd/vsx/vsx.h carries the details):
- movemask is one vbpermq (ISA 2.07) gathering the four word sign bits in
  x86 bit order; all/any/none are record-form compares (vcmpequw.) that
  branch on CR6; masks are canonical all-ones/zero lanes.
- madd/msub/nmadd/nmsub are vec_madd/vec_msub/vec_nmsub/vec_nmadd
  (xvmadd*/xvmsub*/xvnmsub*/xvnmadd*), for vfloat4, Vec3fa, Vec3fx, Vec2fa
  and the scalar helpers (xsmaddasp).  node_intersector1.h and
  node_intersector_packet.h take the fused traversal shape (org*rdir
  precomputed, msub per plane) that upstream enables for AVX2 and NEON.
- shuffles are __builtin_shuffle with a constant mask, so GCC emits the
  single-instruction permutes (xxswapd, xxspltd, xxspltw, xxmrghw/lw,
  vmrgew/ow, xxpermdi); shuffle<1,0,3,2> is a doubleword rotate (vrld 32),
  the word rotations are vec_sld, shift_right_1 is one vsldoi against zero.
  Blends with immediate masks are xxsel with a constant.
- float min/max keep SSE minps/maxps NaN semantics (compare+select: the
  second operand when unordered).  xvminsp/xvmaxsp return the non-NaN
  operand, and the kernels depend on propagation: OBBNode::clear() marks
  empty children with NaN transforms and culls them through
  max(tnear, tNearXYZ) <= min(tfar, tFarXYZ).  With xvminsp those children
  were traversed and embree_verify's regression_static crashed on the
  emptyNode leaf.  mini/maxi (integer min/max on the float bits) are
  vminsw/vmaxsw as on x86.
- vint4(vfloat4) rounds to nearest even (xvrspic + vctsxs) like cvtps2dq.
  vfloat4(vuint4) is one xvcvuxwsp; the SSE tier's two-step trick double
  rounds for values >= 2^31, so this is the correctly rounded one.
- rcp/rsqrt: xvresp/xvrsqrtesp (14.6/15.4 bits, measured) plus one fused
  Newton step (24.0/23.4 bits).  The SSE tier seeds from 12-bit rcpps.
- narrow loads (vfloat4::load(const unsigned char*) etc.) widen with two
  merges against zero or two unpacks, no memory constants;
  vint4::store(unsigned char*) is the SSE packus pair (vpkswus+vpkshus),
  vint4::store(unsigned short*) the modulo pack (vpkuwum) upstream's scalar
  cast implies.
- !=, > and >= are the ordered/unordered IEEE forms the NEON tier uses:
  != is true for NaN operands, > and >= are false (SSE's cmpnlt/cmpnle
  are true).
- Everything lowers to ISA 2.07 at -mcpu=power8 (verified: the
  -mcpu=power8 library decodes identically under objdump -M power8 and
  -M power9); -mcpu=power9 lets GCC pick lxv/stxv, xxinsertw/xxextractuw,
  mtvsrws, lxvwsx for the same builtins.

Verified on POWER9 (GCC 16.1.1, -mcpu=power9): the operation-level
differential probe (powerpc64le-handbook/probes/embree_vsx_probe.cpp) over
32,067 records against the compat-header build: 29,470 bit-identical, 661
within the fused/estimate tolerances, 77 documented (rcp(0), uint->float
rounding), 0 mismatches; embree_verify passes (see packages/embree/README.md);
BMW27 renders at parity with the compat build.

Send to github.com/RenderKit/embree together with embree-ppc64le.patch.

